s... Dissatisfied, Varamos slew his own father, and his guards killed any still loyal to the old elvish king.\n    Varamos, after violently removing the human trade posts, forcibly began to integrate the light elves into his cause. The light elves, after years of their own infighting, finally split between those who supported Varamos and those who didn’t, with the latter fleeing as far as they could.\n    What followed was one of the most violent, bloody periods on all of Mirnos’ history, as Varamos began his horrific conquest across all of Mirnos, with many calling him and his strange dark powers, the greatest threat the realm had ever faced. Shortly after arriving in Newyark, the city went under a surprise siege from Varamos, whose vicious naval power killed both of Newheart’s parents. Orphaned, and sworn to vengeance, Newheart’s life was about to take a dramatic turn...\n    Rhazal Khan, a legendary sellsword, took pity on the angry, orphaned boy. He would go on to not only educate the boy in fighting, but through the help of a powerful mage helped Newheart tap into his deep, mystical power scarcely understood even today. Now a young man, Newheart would go on to have many adventures before he officially joined the Alderian military, but once he did, he quickly built up the trust of not only his men and commanding officers.\n   But soon even the generals heard word of this enigmatic young man and began to speak and praise him for his fighting and quick-thinking abilities. Newheart rose through the ranks at an astonishing rate, and more and more battles were won under his decisive leadership, including his most famous naval battles. The second Battle of the Bay of Valar and the battle on the Black Ocean, as well as several land victories where he aided Ramon in pushing back the Dark Elfish Encroach from their lands.\n    Eventually, with Varamos pushed back now and cornered in Solkai, Newheart was chosen to lead the final assault, and end the mad elvish king’s reign of terror. With great courage and determination, he did not only lead and defeated the Dark Elf Encroach at the famous battle of Solkai. He had also beaten Varamos himself in a one-on-one duel, slaying the dark lord and avenging Newheart's family. Newheart and his companions would go on to become legends, with Newheart granted the title of ‘Protector of the Realm’ by the late King Lorencius, and bestowed numerous titles and land.\n\n    This overview, dear viewer, is but a fraction of Newheart’s story. You can find more books on Newhearts' adventures at your local library, including his defeat of the rebel Orc leader: Kaliban O’ Nok!"

